From 5e5d2b053719c6f441b00765c81c22c673deaf9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hhsnake <hhsnakeg@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 17:28:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] btusb: QCA: pass 0x2EDC debug frames to the monitor

Equivalent of mainline 0b00bee940cb ("Bluetooth: btusb: Reclassify
Qualcomm WCN6855 debug packets"). Mainline reclassifies ACL frames with
handle 0x2EDC as HCI_DIAG_PKT through hdev->classify_pkt_type, which 6.8
does not have; divert them with hci_recv_diag() in btusb_recv_acl_qca()
instead, so they stop showing up as "ACL packet for unknown connection
handle 3804".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
index dde95fd..8f98727 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -3624,6 +3624,14 @@ out:
 
 static int btusb_recv_acl_qca(struct hci_dev *hdev, struct sk_buff *skb)
 {
+	/* Some Qualcomm controllers send debug packets as ACL frames with
+	 * connection handle 0x2EDC; they are not real ACL data. Upstream
+	 * reclassifies them via hdev->classify_pkt_type (0b00bee940cb), which
+	 * 6.8 lacks, so hand them to the monitor as diag packets here.
+	 */
+	if (skb->len >= 2 && get_unaligned_le16(skb->data) == 0x2EDC)
+		return hci_recv_diag(hdev, skb);
+
 	if (acl_pkt_is_dump_qca(hdev, skb))
 		return handle_dump_pkt_qca(hdev, skb);
 	return hci_recv_frame(hdev, skb);
